{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-dilog-convergence","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-dilog-convergence","kind":"proposition","title":"Convergence of the quantum dilogarithm $\\Phi_q$ on $\\lvert z\\rvert < q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-quantum-dilogarithm"],"cites":["references/habiro2004cyclotomic"],"tags":["brane-tower","quantum-dilogarithm","convergence","algebraic-cauchy-limit-half"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.MassEndomorphism.PhiQConvergence.quantumDilog_multipliable","text":"quantum-dilog-convergence.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:quantum-dilog-convergence\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in \\mathbb{R}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1 &#x3C; q</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z \\in \\mathbb{R}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|z| &#x3C; q</code>. Then the quantum dilogarithm</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Phi_q(z) \\;=\\; \\prod_{k \\geq 1} \\bigl(1 - q^{-k} z\\bigr)^{-1}</code></pre>\n<p><em>is multipliable: the infinite product converges to a well-defined, non-zero real number.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/quantum-dilog-convergence.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.5.12"}
